 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls**
-*   **Uninitialized Geometry:** Applying $L_{SVD}$ too early leads to inaccurate plane estimation. The loss scheduling sets $\lambda_1 = 0$ during the first epoch to mitigate this [S1].
-*   **Semantic Ambiguity:** Classes like "wall" or "building" may contain multiple planes. Applying the single-plane assumption to these classes degrades performance. Semantic masking is required to exclude them [S1].
-*   **Low Texture:** Without $L_{dSSIM}$, geometry initialization on low-texture surfaces is poor. The dSSIM term is crucial for this phase [S1].
+*   **Uninitialized Geometry:** Applying $L_{SVD}$ too early leads to inaccurate plane estimation [S1]. The loss scheduling sets $\lambda_1 = 0$ during the first epoch to mitigate this [S1].
+*   **Semantic Ambiguity:** Classes like "wall" or "building" may contain multiple planes [S1]. Applying the single-plane assumption to these classes degrades performance [S1]. Semantic masking is required to exclude them [S1].
+*   **Low Texture:** Without $L_{dSSIM}$, geometry initialization on low-texture surfaces is poor [S1]. The dSSIM term is crucial for this phase [S1].
 
